  "adaptations": [
    "The original reference is concept art. This workspace reproduces its panel composition and primary-color hierarchy with live native controls, not a flattened reference image.",
    "Oscillator algorithm menus expose actual Surge algorithms. Fictional generic Sample tabs and fabricated wavetable names are not painted as working controls.",
    "Oscillator parameter labels and values follow the active algorithm. Algorithm slots that the current patch does not use are disabled rather than attached to unrelated controls.",
    "The upper terrain is a perspective preview of the actual current oscillator waveform, not a claimed real-time three-dimensional spectrum or a sweep of distinct wavetable frames.",
    "The visible amplitude envelope is the real first envelope; the second native envelope and all additional LFO options remain available in Full editor. Four fictitious envelope tabs are not added.",
    "Filter routing uses supported native configurations, balance and feedback. A scene-morph slider is not fabricated; the output section exposes the actual selected scene level.",
    "Eight macro controls are retained. The first effect's real algorithm parameters are visible, with all sixteen native effect slots available in Full editor.",
    "Filter response plots are identified as previews. Output meters read actual signal levels and do not show fabricated activity when the synth is silent.",
    "The shared header retains a functional skin selector, preset navigation, Scene A/B selection and Full editor access instead of copying decorative operating-system chrome.",
    "Colored title strips, white ink on red/blue controls, and ivory effect/macro bodies preserve the concept's contrast while maintaining live accessible child controls.",
    "Scene controls use the reference's full-width stacked label/knob rows. The output area uses a real audio analyzer with compact native master and selected-scene level fields below it; the concept's unsupported A/B morph is not fabricated.",
    "Filter cards now retain three primary rotary controls and a compact KTR field at the reference location. The actual envelope-modulation parameter stays correctly named and is not relabeled as an unsupported per-filter drive."
  ]
}
